---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import site from '../site.config.ts';
---
<Page title="About" description={`About ${site.name}, a free rolling offset calculator for pipe and EMT conduit.`}>
  <p>{site.name} is a free tool for plumbers, pipefitters and electricians. You enter the rise and the roll. It gives you the true offset, the travel, the run and the cut length. In conduit mode it also gives the distance between bends and the shrink.</p>
  <h2>Why we built it</h2>
  <p>Most offset calculators are old pages that are hard to use on a phone. Many of them give only one number, or they hide the answer behind a button. On a job you hold a tape in one hand and a phone in the other. So this page works with one hand, shows the answers as you type, and labels every number on a diagram.</p>
  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <p>The math is plain right-triangle geometry. The true offset is the diagonal of the rise and the roll. The travel is the true offset divided by the sine of the fitting angle. You can read the full steps in the article on the home page.</p>
  <p>The tool runs in your browser. We do not ask you to create an account, and we do not send your measurements anywhere.</p>
  <h2>Check your work</h2>
  <p>The take-off sizes in the table are typical values for common fittings. Fittings differ by maker, so measure yours on jobs where an error costs money. This tool does not replace the code, the plans or your own judgment.</p>
  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>Questions or ideas? Write to <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> or visit the <a href="/contact/">Contact page</a>.</p>
</Page>
